> simplify (x+1)*(x-1)
  ucas: simplify (x+1)*(x-1)
simplify (x + 1)*(x - 1)
  = x^2 - 1
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> simplify x**2 - 1
  ucas: simplify x**2 - 1
simplify x^2 - 1
  = x^2 - 1
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> simplify sin(x)**2 + cos(x)**2
  ucas: trig sin(x)**2 + cos(x)**2
  note: x is taken as real
trig forms of sin(x)**2 + cos(x)**2
  simplified: sin^2 + cos^2 = 1, cosh^2 - sinh^2 = 1, f(f^-1(u)) = u
    = 1
    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 2e-16)
  simplest: 1  (simplified)
> simplify 1/x + 1/y
  ucas: simplify 1/x + 1/y
simplify 1/x + 1/y
  = (x + y)/(x*y)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> simplify (x + y)/(x*y)
  ucas: simplify (x + y)/(x*y)
simplify (x + y)/(x*y)
  = (x + y)/(x*y)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> simplify exp(a)*exp(b)
  ucas: simplify exp(a)*exp(b)
simplify exp(a)*exp(b)
  = exp(a + b)
  check: equal at 64 sample points (max relative difference 3.2e-16)
> simplify abs(x)*abs(x)
  ucas: simplify abs(x)*abs(x)
simplify abs(x)*abs(x)
  = abs(x)^2
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> simplify max(x,y) + min(x,y)
  ucas: simplify max(x,y) + min(x,y)
simplify max(x, y) + min(x, y)
  = max(x, y) + min(x, y)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> simplify I*I
  ucas: simplify I*I
simplify I*I
  = I^2
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> expand (x+1)**2
  ucas: expand (x+1)**2
expand (x + 1)^2
  = x^2 + 2x + 1
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> expand x**2 + 2*x + 1
  ucas: expand x**2 + 2*x + 1
expand x^2 + 2x + 1
  = x^2 + 2x + 1
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> factor x**4 - 1
factor x^4 - 1
  = (x - 1)*(x + 1)*(x^2 + 1)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> factor (x - 1)*(x + 1)*(x**2 + 1)
factor (x - 1)*(x + 1)*(x^2 + 1)
  = (x - 1)*(x + 1)*(x^2 + 1)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> expand (x+2)**3
  ucas: expand (x+2)**3
expand (x + 2)^3
  = x^3 + 6x^2 + 12x + 8
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> factor x**3 + 6*x**2 + 12*x + 8
factor x^3 + 6x^2 + 12x + 8
  = (x + 2)^3
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> simplify x**3 + 6*x**2 + 12*x + 8
  ucas: simplify x**3 + 6*x**2 + 12*x + 8
simplify x^3 + 6x^2 + 12x + 8
  = (x + 2)^3
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> simplify (x + 2)**3
  ucas: simplify (x + 2)**3
simplify (x + 2)^3
  = (x + 2)^3
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
